<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73602" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόζῠγ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>yoked together,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1008d
				</span></i>
			 : metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοιχεῖον,</span> i.e.
			consonant, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				41.381
			</span></i> ; neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόζυγα λατρεύοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					4.602
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>in the same row,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>corresponding,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὁ. κῶλον</span> the
			<i>corresponding</i> limb (on the other side), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).369
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμώνυμα καὶ ὁ.
			[μέρεα],</span> e.g. eyes, hands, feet, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
